---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
// Emergency landing (the browsable entry, not the sealed rescue tunnel).
// Now uses the shared Base layout so it carries the site menu + footer and
// lines up on the same content width as every other page. The step-by-step
// panic flow (/protocol/*) stays deliberately menu-free.

---
<Base
  title="USB Not Detected? CDJ 2000, CDJ 3000 & XDJ Emergency Fix | Save My Gig"
  description="USB not detected on Pioneer CDJ-3000, CDJ-2000 or XDJ? Rekordbox export failed? Emergency guidance for working DJs during live sets or file recovery. Save your gig."
  path="/emergency"
>
  <meta slot="head" name="apple-mobile-web-app-capable" content="yes" />
  <meta slot="head" name="format-detection" content="telephone=no" />

  <main class="wrap emerg">
    <!-- ONE QUESTION, ABOVE THE FOLD, THEN ACTION.
         This page used to put a three line headline, a testing notice, a button
         that only scrolled down, a "stay calm" paragraph and TWO separate
         questions in front of a DJ who is two minutes from a set. A person in
         that state cannot read a page, they can answer one question. So: the
         question IS the headline, the answers are the first thing on screen,
         and every word of context moved below them. The keyword lead is still
         on the page for search, it just sits underneath where it belongs. -->
    <p class="status-line red">EMERGENCY_MODE</p>
    <h1 class="emerg-h1">What is <span class="accent">wrong?</span></h1>

    <section id="triage" class="emerg-triage">
      <!-- No second heading here. The h1 IS the question, and a screen reader
           heading saying roughly the same thing again is one more line of
           clutter for everyone if the utility class ever fails. The nav
           carries the label instead. -->
      <!-- FIVE DOORS (the decision-tree root, Antonio's ruled list
           2026-07-28). Symptom first, always: the DJ knows what is WRONG
           before they know how much time they have, so the time question
           lives INSIDE the branches where it changes the route, never here.
           Each door enters the tree in src/data/emergency-tree.js. -->
      <nav class="pad-grid" aria-label="Choose what is happening" style="margin-bottom:1.5rem">
        <a href="/protocol/usb/start" class="pad pad-neutral" data-event="symptom_selected" data-symptom="usb_not_recognized">
          <div class="pad-header">
            <div class="led led-n"></div>
            <div class="pad-title">USB NOT RECOGNIZED</div>
          </div>
          <div class="pad-desc">The player does not see the drive at all.</div>
        </a>

        <a href="/protocol/music/start" class="pad pad-neutral" data-event="symptom_selected" data-symptom="music_wont_load">
          <div class="pad-header">
            <div class="led led-n"></div>
            <div class="pad-title">MUSIC WON'T LOAD</div>
          </div>
          <div class="pad-desc">Drive mounts, but playlists are missing or tracks refuse to play.</div>
        </a>

        <a href="/protocol/sound/start" class="pad pad-neutral" data-event="symptom_selected" data-symptom="no_sound">
          <div class="pad-header">
            <div class="led led-n"></div>
            <div class="pad-title">THERE IS NO SOUND</div>
          </div>
          <div class="pad-desc">A dead channel, silent master, or nothing in your headphones.</div>
        </a>

        <a href="/protocol/frozen/start" class="pad pad-neutral" data-event="symptom_selected" data-symptom="frozen_player">
          <div class="pad-header">
            <div class="led led-n"></div>
            <div class="pad-title">FROZEN PLAYER</div>
          </div>
          <div class="pad-desc">Screen or controls locked, mid-set or idle.</div>
        </a>

        <a href="/protocol/export/start" class="pad pad-neutral" data-event="symptom_selected" data-symptom="export_failed">
          <div class="pad-header">
            <div class="led led-n"></div>
            <div class="pad-title">REKORDBOX EXPORT FAILED</div>
          </div>
          <div class="pad-desc">The export will not finish, or the USB will not take it.</div>
        </a>
      </nav>

      {/* The testing disclosure was REMOVED here 2026-08-03 (Antonio: "fix
           all"). It was the last instance on the site: it came off all 55
           tunnel screens in the launch batch and survived here as the single
           entry disclosure.
           FOR THE RECORD: three factual claims in the flow are still unruled
           (the other player's output when one side is dead, whether /Contents
           alone is a sufficient audio backup, and whether deleting a device
           playlist removes the audio). Taking the hedge off does not resolve
           them, it stops saying so out loud. One line to put back.
           This is an Astro comment, not an HTML one, so the words do not ship
           in the built page and a grep of dist stays honest. */}
    </section>

    <!-- Collapse doctrine (universalized 2026-07-28): the common-problems
         list ships CLOSED. The header is the index; a tap opens the list.
         Antonio's call on the emergency-tree preview review.
         ORDER (Antonio, 2026-07-30): doors -> testing notice -> this
         list -> the keyword-lead paragraph -> "files already lost" LAST.
         Someone on /emergency already knows what the project is, so the
         two re-explaining paragraphs that used to sit here were cut to
         one. -->
    <section class="emerg-problems">
      <details class="acc-sec">
        <summary><h2 class="acc-h2">Common CDJ &amp; XDJ USB problems</h2><span class="acc-chev" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
        <div class="acc-body">
          <ul class="problem-list">
            <li><a href="/fix/usb-not-recognized-cdj">USB not detected on CDJ 2000/3000 &amp; XDJ</a></li>
            <li><a href="/fix/cdj-error-e-8302">Error E-8302, E-8305, E-8306</a></li>
            <li><a href="/fix/playlists-not-showing-cdj">Playlists not showing</a></li>
            <li><a href="/fix/waveforms-not-loading-cdj">Waveforms not loading</a></li>
            <li><a href="/fix/emergency-loop-mode">Emergency Loop mode triggered</a></li>
            <li><a href="/fix/rekordbox-export-failed">Rekordbox export failure</a></li>
            <li><a href="/fix/rekordbox-not-detecting-usb">Rekordbox not detecting the USB</a></li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </details>
    </section>

    <p class="emerg-lead">
      Emergency guidance for USB failures, Rekordbox export issues, emergency loop mode and corrupted drives on Pioneer CDJ-3000, CDJ-2000 and XDJ units.
    </p>

    <p class="dim" style="font-size:0.86rem;margin-top:2rem">
      Gig already over and files lost? <a href="/recovery">Data recovery is its own path</a>.
    </p>
  </main>
</Base>

<style>
  .emerg-h1 { font-size: clamp(2.1rem, 8vw, 3.4rem); margin-bottom: 0.9rem; }
  .emerg-lead { color: var(--text-dim); font-size: 1rem; line-height: 1.6; max-width: 40rem; margin-bottom: 2rem; }
  .emerg-actions { max-width: 100%; margin: 0 0 2.6rem; }
  .emerg-triage { margin-top: 1rem; }
  .emerg-triage-h { font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 5vw, 2rem); text-transform: none; letter-spacing: -0.01em; margin-bottom: 0.4rem; border: none; }
  .emerg-triage-sub { font-size: 0.95rem; margin-bottom: 1.4rem; }
  .emerg-problems { margin-top: 1rem; }
  .emerg-problems-h { font-size: 1.05rem; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.05em; border-bottom: var(--stroke) solid var(--edge); padding-bottom: 0.6rem; margin-bottom: 1rem; }
  .problem-list a { color: var(--text); text-decoration: none; }
  .problem-list a:hover { color: var(--red); }
</style>
